  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a connected undirected acyclic graph with NNN vertices numbered 111 to NNN, or in short, a tree. You are also given a parameter KKK such that 1≤K≤21 \\le K \\le 21≤K≤2.\n\nLet dist(X,Y)dist(X, Y)dist(X,Y) denote the distance between the nodes XXX and YYY, or more formally, the number of edges on the unique simple path from XXX to YYY.\n\nFor 333 distinct vertices, XXX, YYY and ZZZ, we define f(X,Y,Z)f(X, Y, Z)f(X,Y,Z) as the minimum value of dist(A,X)+dist(A,Y)+dist(A,Z)dist(A, X) + dist(A, Y) + dist(A, Z)dist(A,X)+dist(A,Y)+dist(A,Z) over all 1≤A≤N1 \\le A \\le N1≤A≤N.\n\nYour task is to find the sum of (4⋅f(X,Y,Z)K)(4 \\cdot f(X, Y, Z)^K)(4⋅f(X,Y,Z)K) over all triplets  satisfying 1≤X&lt;Y&lt;Z≤N1 \\le X &lt; Y &lt; Z \\le N1≤X&lt;Y&lt;Z≤N. Since the answer may be large, print it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\nThe iii-th of the next N−1N - 1N−1 lines contains 222 integers - uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, representing an edge in the tree.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput ∑(4⋅f(X,Y,Z)K)\\sum (4 \\cdot f(X, Y, Z)^K)∑(4⋅f(X,Y,Z)K) over all 1≤X&lt;Y&lt;Z≤N1 \\le X &lt; Y &lt; Z \\le N1≤X&lt;Y&lt;Z≤N modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤K≤21 \\le K \\le 21≤K≤2",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "It is guaranteed that the input edges form a valid tree.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (4 points):** K=1,N≤50,ui=i,vi=i+1K = 1, N \\le 50, u_i = i, v_i = i + 1K=1,N≤50,ui​=i,vi​=i+1.",
      "**Subtask 2 (7 points):** K=1,N≤50K = 1, N \\le 50K=1,N≤50.",
      "**Subtask 3 (13 points):** K=1,N≤400K = 1, N \\le 400K=1,N≤400.",
      "**Subtask 4 (17 points):** K=1,N≤3000K = 1, N \\le 3000K=1,N≤3000.",
      "**Subtask 5 (24 points):** K=1K = 1K=1.",
      "**Subtask 6 (35 points):** K=2K = 2K=2."
    ],
